   465	making conditional reliability look better. Neither is a production incident
   466	rate or proof of absence of bugs.
   467	If an arm accepts nothing, its conditional defect rate is undefined, not
   468	zero; comparisons requiring that rate cannot pass. Freeze conservative
   469	handling of other undefined ratios in M4 rather than dropping those draws.
   470	
   471	### 6.2 Pass requires all gates, against both A and B
   472	
   473	| Gate | Required outcome for Calor |
   474	|---|---|
   475	| Economic advantage (primary) | Upper confidence bound on cost-per-correct-acceptance ratio <= 0.50 versus each C# arm |
   476	| Useful completion | Lower confidence bound on Calor correctly accepted fraction >= 80%, and on its difference versus each C# arm >= -5 percentage points |
   477	| Safety non-inferiority | Upper confidence bound on Calor minus each C# arm serious-defect rate <= +1 percentage point, for both all-assigned and accepted denominators |
   478	| Trust boundary | No confirmed false-established property or accepted unauthorized boundary bypass in the frozen mechanism suite or confirmatory runs |
   479	| Usable adoption | Independent adopter completes install, integration, a change, and an export-to-C# handoff; all effort and loss of guarantees disclosed |
   480	
   481	The +1 percentage point safety allowance is a proposed non-inferiority
   482	margin, **not "no extra risk"**. The adopter must explicitly accept it before
   483	pilot collection; unacceptable risk means no experiment under this proposal.
   484	Report absolute rates and intervals alongside relative differences.
   485	**Error control is across the two positive decision branches.** Allocate
   486	alpha = 0.025 to LANGUAGE EARNS CONTINUATION and alpha = 0.025 to WORKFLOW
   487	VALUE. Within each branch, every statistical component must pass at that
   488	branch's level: use valid **one-sided 97.5% bounds**, including pessimistic
   489	registered cost inputs. The branch is an intersection-union test; if any
   490	required component is false, passing the entire conjunction has probability
   491	at most 0.025. No further within-branch multiplicity penalty is needed.
   492	
   493	The union bound therefore limits any false positive branch claim to 5%,
   494	without assuming independent components or branches. Section 8's precedence
   495	selects the reported outcome; precedence alone is not error control. These
   496	are decision bounds, **not simultaneous confidence coverage** of every
   497	quantity. Descriptive 95% intervals may also be shown but cannot adjudicate
   498	the gates. M4 validates the estimators under the actual clustered design.
   499	See [intersection-union theorem 17.3](https://bookdown.org/jkang37/stat205b-notes/lecture13.html#thm:thm17003).
   500	
   501	Review time, agent iterations, context read, and prevented violations are
   502	secondary explanations. Neither a fivefold point-estimate defect reduction
   503	nor a better token score can rescue failure of the primary economic route.
