   608	
   609	### 6.4 No optional stopping or convenient restarts
   610	
   611	Fix sample counts and collection dates at M4. No early stopping for a win,
   612	no outcome-based sample extension, and no harvesting the best task subset.
   613	Stop immediately for a trust-boundary defect or at the spending ceiling.
   614	Publish incomplete counts and costs; stopped collection cannot pass.
   615	
   616	For a protocol defect, publish the defect and identify affected evidence.
   617	Do not patch the compiler and keep favorable old runs. A replacement epoch
   618	requires fresh preregistration, unseen tasks where leakage occurred, and
