   642	| Historical supply and consent | Adopter engineering lead: confirm inventory, workload horizon, research agreement and exit promises in M1. |
   643	| Correctness follow-through | Compiler maintainer: record ownership/disposition of the false-established search even if comparison work stops. |
   644	
   645	Enter actual assignee names and dated decisions in the authorization record;
   646	these roles are not claims that anyone has agreed. Missing required approval
   647	blocks that action. M1 review-only entry under a conditional M0 output may
   648	address requirements or bounded information requests, not start M2-M4.
   649	
   650	If the original comparison is not feasible, record that before considering
   651	an **exploratory option**. A separate proposal must name one uncertainty,
   652	the smallest artifact needed, a fixed dataset, allowed claims, a time/spend
   653	ceiling, and a stop decision. Prefer existing tools and an in-house example.
   654	A friction study can estimate human minutes and repair costs; a mechanism
   655	probe can find false guarantees. Neither can pass section 6, downgrade its
   656	safety gate to descriptive reporting, cross Call 3, or authorize full
   657	section 4 implementation. A promising exploration may justify proposing a
   658	new study, not automatically continuing language investment.
   659	Maintainer-only timings must be labeled **author time**, not adopter review
   660	savings. Any external-review-time claim needs a non-maintainer participant
   661	and must still disclose the exploratory sample and its limits.
