   238	### 7.3 Pre-registered reachability in the public-proxy domain
   239	
   240	G0, G1.1, G1.2, G5, and G6.2 are `NOT_MEASURABLE_IN_DOMAIN`. Therefore rules 3
   241	and 4 **cannot be satisfied** in the public-proxy domain under v1. The
   242	reachable results are:
   243	
   244	- **NOT FEASIBLE (AI-adjudicated, public-proxy domain; frame-scoped)** through
   245	  rule 2;
   246	- **INSUFFICIENT INFORMATION (AI-adjudicated, public-proxy domain)** through
   247	  rule 5;
   248	- process status **UNADJUDICATED** through rule 1.
   249	
   250	This outcome space is stated before any evidence is inspected. The public-proxy
   251	substitution cannot produce a positive classification; reaching one requires a
   252	later rules version that adds an evidence source able to measure G0, G1, G5,
   253	and G6.2 as originally defined.
   254	
   255	### 7.4 Method-independent necessary cluster count (supply route)
   256	
   257	For the safety component G3.1 of either branch, with margin +1 pp,
   258	alpha = 0.025, target power 0.80, and the most-favorable registered
   259	alternative (subject minus comparator = -1 pp; section 4.3), any valid
   260	level-0.025 test of the composite null has power at that alternative no greater
   261	than the Neyman-Pearson most powerful test of one null point against it. The
   262	null point shifts only the subject arm's escape probability from `c` to
   263	`c + 0.02`, which lies on the null boundary. Each source cluster contributes one
   264	independent binary observation per arm (Draft v3 section 5.1; validity over
   265	arbitrary within-cluster dependence, section 4.2). Coherence limits `c` to
   266	`[0, 0.05]`, because a serious escape implies an accepted but not correctly
   267	accepted artifact and the most-favorable subject correct-acceptance
   268	probability is 0.95.
   269	
   270	`N_MIN` is the minimum over that `c` grid (step 0.001) of the smallest cluster
   271	count at which the most powerful test reaches power 0.80. The frozen
   272	calculator [r1-safety-nmin.py](r1-safety-nmin.py) gives **`N_MIN = 172`**,
   273	attained at `c = 0` (where it equals `ceil(ln(0.025/0.80) / ln(0.98))`).
   274	
   275	**Rule:** G3.1 is `SIZED_INFEASIBLE` (in both branches) if and only if
   276	`F_high` is finite and `F_high < N_MIN`, that is, `H_high <= 128`.
   277	
   278	Why this route is valid in the proxy domain: the bound does not depend on how
   279	acceptance or escapes are ascertained, on reviewer type, cost, or any nuisance
   280	parameter other than `c`, which it minimizes over. It holds for any binary
   281	per-cluster escape endpoint with this margin, including the original one. What
   282	it scopes is the **supply**: it shows that a study drawing its final pool from
   283	the frozen frame cannot be powered, not that an adopter-domain study could not.
   284	Pilot reservations are taken as zero and authored clusters at their 25% cap,
   285	both favorable to feasibility. Larger true safety advantages than -1 pp would
   286	lower `N_MIN`; -1 pp is the registered most-favorable alternative, fixed before
   287	inspection, and cannot be changed after inspection (section 10).
